  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting Relevant Context**\n\nI\'m now diving into the latest information, specifically the details from `references/3_saas_dashboard.md`, to connect the existing knowledge with the frontend design domain. I\'m also quickly verifying the environment setup with `python3 --version` and `node` to ensure all relevant tools are in place.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating Project Scope**\n\nI\'m now reconsidering the initial approach, focusing on the user\'s explicit directive to start with PHASE 1 and not stop at the design or planning stage. I\'m carefully reviewing the requirements and the context from `cloudsql-setup/SKILL.md` to ensure a holistic understanding before initiating any implementation steps. My primary aim is to align with the specific instructions provided.\n\n\n**Prioritizing AI Studio Build**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the AI Studio Build flow. The directive to stop and yield after `show_aistudio_ui` has thrown a wrench in my plans! I\'m carefully weighing whether to integrate a minimal Phase 1 with a working local persistence, or stop at an early state. The goal is to fully deliver a meaningful Phase 1, given the \"stop and yield\" constraint and the user\'s focus on a working, complete PHASE 1.\n\n\n**Clarifying PHASE 1 Scope**\n\nI\'m now firmly focused on building a fully functional Phase 1, avoiding any Cloud SQL interaction or npm package installations (like `drizzle-orm` or `pg`) as per the consent gate and `cloudsql-setup/SKILL.md`. I realize that even showing a blank screen with a Cloud SQL popup violates the \"start implementation\" directive. My next steps are to confirm the environment setup, read `references/3_saas_dashboard.md`, and aim for a complete Phase 1 implementation.\n\n\n**Confirming Functional Pillars**\n\nI\'m now carefully re-evaluating the scope of Phase 1, given the \"complete application\" directive. My plan includes a functional offline foundation (ie.js), an Express API backend with RBAC and audit logging, and interactive views for the core functionalities (Prevent, Detect, Protect, Offline Sync, Reports, Appointments, Referrals, and Simulink Analytics). I\'m also ensuring zero dead buttons or empty screens. Furthermore, I\'ll explicitly document PostgreSQL Cloud SQL provisioning and migrations as a Phase 5 task. I am going back to re-read the prompt to be absolutely sure!\n\n\n**Defining Phase 1\'s Finish**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on delivering a truly complete Phase 1. I\'m prioritizing its scope: architecture, setup, design, navigation, dashboards, auth/RBAC, bilingual support (EN/TA), and a PWA/Dexie offline foundation. My aim is to build a deeply functional, production-ready system, and the reference image will guide the design. I\'m committed to ensuring Phase 1 is fully polished and meets the user\'s expectations.\n\n\n**Implementing Interconnected Modules**\n\nI\'m now striving to make sure every navigation element and action in the sidebar and dashboards function. Each module must open an interconnected, interactive entity, sharing live state stored in IndexedDB (Dexie.js), and synchronized with the backend. This includes RBAC, audit logging, and a SQL/PostgreSQL schema blueprint. The complete connected journey is the focus.\n\n\n\n"
