  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Style**\n\nI\'ve begun examining the uploaded image, focusing on its visual style. Specifically, I\'m observing the deep navy-teal sidebar color, noting its hex code. I\'m taking a careful inventory of its design components and the overall aesthetic the graphic artist is trying to convey. I\'ll need to expand my analysis, but so far I am making good progress.\n\n\n**Detailing Aesthetic Components**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the aesthetic components. I am noting the use of specific hex codes, such as `#0B3954`, and their application within the gradient surfaces. I\'m seeing a clean design with a Mritidhristi logo, a clear navigation bar with several options, and a clean footer callout. The main workspace employs off-white and slate colors. Typography choices seem accessible. The top bar houses search, connectivity status, notification triggers, and a language selector.\n\n\n**Outlining Dashboard Elements**\n\nI\'m currently outlining the main dashboard\'s components. I\'ve broken it down into a hero welcome banner, quick-launch cards for prevention, detection, and protection, and data rows showcasing health overview and retinal screening results. I envision specific CTAs for exploring health, viewing reports, and reviewing Grad-CAM data. I have finalized a role/profile menu and the PWA install button and the navigation bar and footer elements.\n\n\n**Defining Dashboard Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the dashboard elements for the prevention program. I\'m visualizing a donut progress ring, phase checklists, and a \"Continue Programme\" button. I\'m also planning for upcoming appointments, quick action buttons, and health insights at the bottom. I\'m structuring the right panel for alerts, offline readiness, and a Simulink preview. Additionally, I\'m beginning to map out the dashboard requirements for the doctor and healthcare worker roles, including AI retinal screenings and workflow functions.\n\n\n**Mapping District Metrics**\n\nI\'m now detailing the District Administrator dashboard. I\'m focusing on key metrics like registered patients, assessment completion rates, and screening throughput. I\'m planning for charts on healthcare resource utilization using Recharts, plus Simulink integration. I\'ll need to figure out integration with patient data!\n\n**Checking Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'m reviewing necessary packages for the applet. I have the single `install_applet_package` call: I need Recharts for data visualization, dexie for offline IndexedDB storage, vite-plugin-pwa for PWA features, and zod for strict input validation. Also, I must ensure proper import/export with CSV of Simulink runs.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Policy**\n\nI\'ve hit a key design constraint: I *must* avoid automatic image generation, as per the explicit instruction. I\'m now pivoting to focus on clinical SVG graphics and HTML5 `<canvas>` renderings for retinal fundus images instead. This opens doors for real-time pixel-level image quality checks, advanced illumination corrections, and anatomical overlays. This offers enhanced functionality and image control, and is a better solution. I\'m also planning to create SVG and PNG icons within `public/`.\n\n\n**Validating PWA Compliance**\n\nI\'m now generating all the required PWA assets: the manifest and icons (including `pwa-192x192.png`, `pwa-512x512.png`, `pwa-maskable-512x512.png`, and `apple-touch-icon.png`) using a Node script to make it all 100% valid.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the server architecture and security guidelines. I\'m focusing on the runtime server (`server.ts`), which is an Express server. In development, it will use Vite middleware on port 3000 (via `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"`). In production, it will serve the `dist/` folder via `\"start\": \"tsx server.ts\"` if needed; otherwise, I will test `\"node server.ts\"` to check our framework constraints.\n\n\n**Defining Server Architecture**\n\nI\'m now detailing the server architecture and security measures. The Express server (`server.ts`) will handle requests. It supports authentication routes (`/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/logout`, etc.) with secure password hashing via `crypto.scryptSync`. To ease demos, initial logins use seeded synthetic accounts. Security is paramount, and RBAC with bearer token enforcement will be strict across all API endpoints.\n\n\n**Securing Access Points**\n\nI\'m now implementing robust authentication and authorization. I\'ll default into a synthetic patient session for immediate dashboard access. There will also be a role and account switcher and login, which manages authenticated session exchanges with strict backend RBAC on all API endpoints. Zod will be used for input validation on all routes, with safe file upload validation for retinal images.\n\n\n**Implementing Offline Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating an offline-first architecture. This includes `vite-plugin-pwa` for Workbox precaching and Dexie.js (`src/offline/db.ts`) for storing local records such as patient data, assessments, habit logs, and cached reports. I\'m also preparing to create the mechanism for an audit log. I need to handle pending actions from offline mutations.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "sbQCa6-POv2kkdUPy9jD-AQ"
