  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request**: Design and build **MRITIDHRISTI \342\200\223 PREVENT \342\200\242 DETECT \342\200\242 PROTECT**, a complete, integrated, offline-first, AI-assisted healthcare screening and continuity-of-care support platform prototype connecting:\n  1. **PREVENT** \342\200\224 Type 2 diabetes lifestyle risk (9-input one-question-at-a-time assessment, experimental risk scoring, What-If simulator, clinical HbA1c/FPG testing guidance, 12-month prevention programme Phase 1 Learning & Phase 2 Maintenance, Indian food guidance, daily habits, deterministic adaptive intervention ladder, patient registration & informed consent in English/Tamil with Hindi architecture ready).\n  2. **DETECT** \342\200\224 AI-assisted diabetic retinopathy screening for diagnosed diabetes patients (image acquisition + validation, 7-step retinal pipeline: Step 1 Quality Gate/rejection, Step 2 CLAHE preprocessing, Step 3 Anatomy, Step 4 Lesion detection [illustrative/experimental], Step 5 5-class ICDR grading with safe withholding & OOD detection, Step 6 Grad-CAM explainability with limitations, Step 7 Annotated report; plus dataset governance specs for APTOS 2019, IDRiD, DRIVE, Messidor-2).\n  3. **PROTECT** \342\200\224 Doctor-led clinical coordination (shared longitudinal patient record, doctor review Confirm/Reject/Recapture + clinician-approved triage protocols, referral management, appointment scheduling/attendance/missed escalation, continuity-of-care health-worker follow-ups).\n  4. **Offline-First PWA** \342\200\224 Installable PWA (Service Worker + Web App Manifest + in-app install button), Dexie.js IndexedDB caching of minimized permitted data, offline action queue with idempotency deduplication, synchronization engine, explicit offline vs. online-only boundaries, demonstrable offline test workflow.\n  5. **District Resource Planning (MATLAB Simulink)** \342\200\224 6 district-level scenarios (Normal, High Patient Volume, Limited Connectivity, Camera Shortage, Ophthalmologist Shortage, Increased Referral Demand), comparison charts, explicitly labelled illustrative simulation mode, and documented MATLAB Simulink CSV import interface.\n  6. **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) & Security** \342\200\224 Three role-based dashboards (**Patient**, **Doctor / Healthcare Worker**, **District Administrator**) with permissions enforced on backend APIs, salted `scrypt` password hashing, in-memory `Authorization: Bearer` session tokens, Zod validation, safe image upload validation, and audit trails.\n- **Visual Reference**: User uploaded `/public/assets/aistudio/image_dffbe40e.png` (deep navy-teal collapsible sidebar, clean white/slate-50 healthcare SaaS cards, Patient Dashboard layout with Welcome Hero, 3 Pillar launch cards, Health Overview chart, Retinal Screening Result + Grad-CAM preview, Prevention Programme progress ring, Upcoming Appointments, Quick Actions, Health Insights, and right operational rail).\n- **Phase Instruction**: User specified phased delivery (\"Begin with PHASE 1. Inspect the available environment, explain the architecture briefly and start implementation. Do not stop after creating a design or plan\") and requested `PROJECT_PROGRESS.md`. To guarantee zero dead buttons and a complete end-to-end connected journey on Turn 1, all core UI views, backend APIs, offline Dexie engine, 7-step canvas retinal pipeline, and Simulink analytics have been implemented while keeping Phase 5 Cloud SQL (PostgreSQL) provisioning deferred until user approval.\n- **Hard Media Constraint**: `[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]` explicitly forbids invoking `generate_image` unless the user explicitly asks to create/modify an image. Do NOT call `generate_image`.\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Skills & Docs Read\n- Read `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md` and `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/3_saas_dashboard.md`.\n- Read `/skills/system_skills/pwa_integration/SKILL.md`.\n- Read `/skills/system_skills/securecoder_persona/SKILL.md`.\n- Read `/skills/system_skills/cloudsql-setup/SKILL.md` (confirmed strict consent gate \342\200\224 did NOT install `pg`/`drizzle-orm` or trigger `cloudsql_setup` UI on Turn 1 so we didn\'t block Phase 1 implementation; PostgreSQL schema blueprint created in `/docs/database/schema.sql` for Phase 5).\n- Inspected `/package.json` and runtime environment (`node v22.23.2`, `npm 10.9.8`, `Python 3.11.2`).\n\n### Packages Installed & Config Updated\n- Installed packages via `install_applet_package`: `recharts`, `dexie`, `vite-plugin-pwa`, `zod`.\n- Updated `/metadata.json` with Mritidhristi name and description.\n- Updated `/index.html` with title, OG/meta tags, Google Fonts (`Plus Jakarta Sans`, `DM Sans`, `JetBrains Mono`), and PWA/iOS meta tags (`apple-touch-icon.png`, `icon.svg`, `theme-color`).\n- Updated `/vite.config.ts` adding `VitePWA` (`devOptions: { enabled: true, type: \'module\' }`, manifest with `id`, `start_url`, `scope`, `display: \'standalone\'`, 192/512/maskable icons, Workbox runtime caching) while preserving existing `react`, `tailwindcss`, `copy-unbundled-src-assets`, and `DISABLE_HMR` settings.\n- Updated `/tsconfig.json` adding `\"vite-plugin-pwa/client\"` to `compilerOptions.types`.\n- Updated `/package.json` scripts: `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"`, `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"`.\n- Updated `/src/index.css` with Tailwind v4 `@theme` design tokens, tabular numerals, and `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n- Generated PWA icon assets in `/public/`: `icon.svg`, `pwa-192x192.png`, `pwa-512x512.png`, `pwa-maskable-512x512.png` (padded safe zone), and `apple-touch-icon.png` (180\303\227180).\n\n### Files Created & Completed (Code Written, Not Yet Compiled/Verified)\n- `/src/types/domain.ts` \342\200\224 Full TypeScript domain models covering all 26 entities.\n- `/src/i18n/translations.ts` \342\200\224 English (`en`) and Tamil (`ta`) UI dictionaries + Hindi (`hi`) architecture scaffold.\n- `/server/clinicalLogic.ts` \342\200\224 Experimental rule-based 9-input risk engine, ICMR/ADA HbA1c & FPG interpreter, deterministic 5-step adaptive intervention ladder (isolated pre-approved educational arms), and 6-scenario Simulink-compatible district capacity engine.\n- `/server/store.ts` \342\200\224 Persistent JSON file store (`data/mritidhristi_store.json`), synthetic seed dataset (3 patients, 3 demo roles, assessments, labs, programmes, habits, screenings, reviews, referrals, appointments, follow-ups, notifications, district resources, audit logs), `crypto.scryptSync` + `timingSafeEqual` password hashing, in-memory session TTL map, and immutable audit log writer.\n- `/server.ts` \342\200\224 Express server on port `3000` mounting Vite middleware in dev (`dist/` in prod), strict Zod validation, `requireAuth` + `requireRole` RBAC middleware + patient ownership checks, safe retinal image data-URL validation, all REST endpoints (`/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, `/api/bootstrap`, `/api/patients`, `/api/prevent/*`, `/api/clinical/labs`, `/api/detect/screenings`, `/api/protect/*`, `/api/notifications/:id/read`, `/api/sync/batch`, `/api/admin/simulink/import`, `/api/audit-logs`).\n- `/src/offline/db.ts` \342\200\224 Dexie.js `MritidhristiOfflineDB` storing minimized permitted summaries (`patients`, `assessments`, `habitLogs`, `cachedReports`, `pendingActions`, `syncHistory`). Never stores auth tokens.\n- `/src/offline/syncEngine.ts` \342\200\224 Offline action queueing with unique `idempotencyKey` and batch synchronization to `/api/sync/batch` handling duplicate prevention and conflicts.\n- `/src/hooks/usePWAInstall.ts` \342\200\224 PWA install hook supporting Chromium `beforeinstallprompt`, standalone detection, and iOS Safari guide.\n- `/src/utils/riskEngine.ts` \342\200\224 Client-side offline mirror of experimental 9-input lifestyle risk scoring and What-If calculation.\n- `/src/utils/retinalPipeline.ts` \342\200\224 HTML5 Canvas procedural fundus renderer (Normal Grade 0, Moderate NPDR, Ungradable Blur) + real pixel-level Step 1 Quality Gate (Laplacian sharpness, luminance, exposure clipping, resolution, retinal color OOD check) + CLAHE/anatomy/lesion/Grad-CAM visualization + conservative grade withholding.\n- `/src/components/Sidebar.tsx` \342\200\224 Collapsible deep navy-teal sidebar with mobile drawer and role-aware links.\n- `/src/components/TopBar.tsx` \342\200\224 Search bar, real online/offline + Offline Test Mode toggle, EN/TA/HI language switcher, in-app PWA install button + iOS guide modal, notifications dropdown, profile/role switcher button.\n- `/src/components/FundusVisualizer.tsx` \342\200\224 Reusable canvas visualizer for raw, preprocessed, anatomy, lesion, and Grad-CAM retinal imaging stages.\n- `/src/components/AuthModal.tsx` \342\200\224 Synthetic Role Demos switcher (Patient/Doctor/Admin), scrypt Email/Password login, and new account registration.\n- `/src/views/PatientDashboard.tsx` \342\200\224 Reference-aligned Patient Dashboard with Recharts Health Overview, Fundus + Grad-CAM preview, Prevention ring, Appointments, Quick Actions, Insights, and Right Operational Rail.\n- `/src/views/DoctorDashboard.tsx` \342\200\224 Clinician command center with 4 KPIs, unreviewed retinal screenings queue, missed/escalated visits, and searchable shared patient registry.\n- `/src/views/AdminDashboard.tsx` \342\200\224 District Administrator analytics with data provenance transparency, 5 KPIs, Recharts facility utilization & Simulink comparison charts, and security audit trail.\n- `/src/views/PreventModule.tsx` \342\200\224 Full Pillar 1 (9-input wizard, What-If explorer, 12-month programme + lessons + daily habits + adaptive ladder, clinical HbA1c/FPG guidance & doctor lab entry, patient registration & informed consent).\n- `/src/views/DetectModule.tsx` \342\200\224 Full Pillar 2 (patient eligibility notice, upload + 3 demo presets, interactive 7-step pipeline stepper & canvas inspector, Grad-CAM side-by-side & opacity slider, dataset specs, screening history).\n- `/src/views/ProtectModule.tsx` \342\200\224 Full Pillar 3 (longitudinal summary, Doctor clinical review & triage sign-off, referral creation/tracking/completion, appointments booking/confirmation/missed escalation, continuity health-worker follow-ups).\n- `/src/views/ReportsView.tsx` \342\200\224 Unified printable/exportable reports hub.\n- `/src/views/OfflineSyncView.tsx` \342\200\224 Live Dexie.js inspector, 4-step offline test workflow guide, pending queue, sync history, offline vs. online-only capability matrix, server audit logs.\n- `/src/views/SimulinkAnalyticsView.tsx` \342\200\224 6-scenario district simulator, hourly queue curves, cross-scenario charts, downloadable CSV template, Admin-only Simulink CSV importer.\n- `/src/views/SettingsAndNotificationsView.tsx` \342\200\224 Notifications Center + Settings with EN/TA/HI language selector and live Backend RBAC Verification tester button.\n- `/src/App.tsx` \342\200\224 Root shell wiring auth, offline auto-sync, PWA SW registration, and all views.\n- `/docs/database/schema.sql` \342\200\224 26-table PostgreSQL relational DDL blueprint.\n- `/PROJECT_PROGRESS.md` \342\200\224 Living project progress document.\n\n### Not Yet Executed (Must Run Next!)\n- Have **NOT** yet run `compile_applet` + `lint_applet`!\n- Have **NOT** yet called `restart_dev_server` (needed because `package.json` `\"dev\"` script changed from `vite` to `tsx server.ts`).\n- Have **NOT** yet tested live API endpoints, RBAC enforcement, offline sync batch endpoint, or checked `server.ts` Node 22 compatibility / `npm audit`.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Node 22 + Express Full-Stack**: Runtime is Node v22.23.2; `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` runs Express + Vite middleware on port `3000`. Note: check if `server.ts` has any TypeScript syntax that Node 22 native stripping dislikes if `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"` is ever invoked (standard `import type` and interfaces are cleanly stripped in Node 22; verify with `node --check` or quick check if needed).\n- **Zero Dead Buttons**: In `App.tsx`, `appointments` and `referrals` sidebar links currently route to `ProtectModule` which defaults `subTab` to `\'review\'`! **Improvement needed**: pass an `initialTab` prop to `ProtectModule` (or sync `subTab` from `activeView`) so clicking **Appointments** in the sidebar lands directly on the Appointments tab and clicking **Referrals** lands directly on the Referrals tab!\n- **Same-Turn Security Audit (`securecoder-persona`)**: Because `package.json` dependencies were added (`recharts`, `dexie`, `vite-plugin-pwa`, `zod`), check whether `package-lock.json` or `bun.lock` exists and run read-only audit (`npm audit` or `bun audit`) if a lockfile exists. Also double-check all new files for XSS, path traversal, auth boundaries, and no hardcoded secrets.\n- **Clinical & Scientific Honesty**: All experimental/illustrative outputs (lifestyle risk score, retinal prototype grading, contextual-bandit educational framing, illustrative Simulink mode) are explicitly labelled non-diagnostic / illustrative; no clinical accuracy or weights are fabricated.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Filesystem Timeout Error**: During parallel `write_to_file` of `PreventModule.tsx`, `DetectModule.tsx`, and `ProtectModule.tsx` in the previous turn, the workspace filesystem timed out (`Timed out waiting for applet file system condition to be met`). After the retry turn, `list_dir` succeeded immediately and all three files (`PreventModule.tsx`, `DetectModule.tsx`, `ProtectModule.tsx`) plus `ReportsView.tsx`, `OfflineSyncView.tsx`, `SimulinkAnalyticsView.tsx`, `SettingsAndNotificationsView.tsx`, `App.tsx`, `docs/database/schema.sql`, and `PROJECT_PROGRESS.md` were written cleanly with zero errors.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- All source files are written in `/src/`, `/server/`, `/server.ts`, `/public/`, `/docs/database/schema.sql`, and `/PROJECT_PROGRESS.md`.\n- The dev server has NOT been restarted since `\"dev\"` in `package.json` was changed to `\"tsx server.ts\"` \342\200\224 so `restart_dev_server` MUST be called after verifying compilation!\n- Note: `.gitignore` should ignore `/data/mritidhristi_store.json` if desired (optional check).\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **Fix `ProtectModule` initial sub-tab wiring (small surgical edit)**:\n   - Update `/src/views/ProtectModule.tsx` to accept `initialTab?: \'review\' | \'referrals\' | \'appointments\' | \'continuity\'` and sync `subTab` via `useEffect` when `initialTab` changes.\n   - Update `/src/App.tsx` to pass `initialTab={activeView === \'appointments\' ? \'appointments\' : activeView === \'referrals\' ? \'referrals\' : \'review\'}` to `<ProtectModule />` so sidebar clicks on **Appointments** and **Referrals** jump directly to their respective tabs.\n2. **Co-execute Build & Lint Verification**:\n   - Call `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in the same turn.\n   - Fix any TypeScript, Vite PWA, or bundling errors if reported (max 3 attempts).\n3. **Restart Dev Server & Live Verify**:\n   - Call `restart_dev_server` so the updated `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` Express + Vite server starts cleanly on port `3000`.\n   - Run a quick verification command via `run_command` to:\n     - Test `/api/health` (`200 OK`).\n     - Test `/api/auth/demo-session` (`patient` role) -> test `/api/bootstrap` (`200 OK`) -> test `/api/audit-logs` as `patient` (verify HTTP `403 Forbidden` backend RBAC enforcement!).\n     - Test `/api/auth/demo-session` (`doctor` role) -> test `/api/audit-logs` (`200 OK`) and confirm `RBAC_ACCESS_DENIED` was recorded in the audit trail.\n     - Test `/api/sync/batch` twice with the same `idempotencyKey` to verify `synced` then `duplicate_skipped`.\n     - Check lockfile presence and run read-only `npm audit` (or `bun audit`) per `securecoder-persona`.\n4. **Final Review & Concise Phase 1 Completion Report**:\n   - Present a clear, scannable, builder-friendly summary covering:\n     - Environment inspection & modular architecture overview.\n     - Files created/modified across Phase 1 + interconnected prototype modules.\n     - Verified safeguards (2\342\200\2233 plain-language bullets per `securecoder-persona`, no internal jargon like `SecureCoder` or `CWE`).\n     - How to verify each feature (Role switching, Prevent 9-input & What-If, Detect 7-step pipeline + Ungradable rejection + Grad-CAM, Protect Doctor Review & Triage, Offline Test Mode & Sync deduplication, Simulink 6 scenarios & CSV import, Backend RBAC check).\n     - Explicit note on what is Simulated/Experimental vs. Pending (including readiness to proceed with Phase 5 Cloud SQL PostgreSQL provisioning when requested).\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **No `generate_image`**: Explicitly prohibited by `[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]` unless user explicitly requests image creation.\n- **No Cloud SQL Provisioning Yet**: Do not call `CheckFeatureEligibility` / `show_aistudio_ui(cloudsql_setup)` or install `pg`/`drizzle-orm` unless the user asks to proceed with Phase 5 hosted PostgreSQL setup.\n- **SecureCoder Communication Rule**: Keep security analysis internal; in chat, summarize 2\342\200\2233 verified safeguards in plain language without jargon (`CWE`, `SSRF`, `SecureCoder`, etc.).\n- **Clinical Honesty**: Never claim diagnostic accuracy, real CNN weights, validated risk prediction, or live MATLAB execution. Clearly label synthetic data, experimental rules, and illustrative simulation outputs.\n- **Communication Style**: Concise, scannable, action-oriented, no hype, no internal step IDs.\n</summary>"
