  planner_response {
    response: "**MRITIDHRISTI \342\200\223 PREVENT \342\200\242 DETECT \342\200\242 PROTECT** has been built and verified as an integrated, offline-first, role-based healthcare screening and continuity-of-care prototype.\n\n### Architecture Overview\n- **Frontend**: React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS v4, Recharts, Lucide icons, and Dexie.js (IndexedDB) configured as an installable Progressive Web App (`vite-plugin-pwa` + Workbox Service Worker + Web App Manifest).\n- **Backend**: Node.js + Express REST API on port `3000` serving the SPA, Zod request validation, role-based access control (`patient`, `doctor`, `admin`), salted `scrypt` password hashing, in-memory Bearer sessions, persistent JSON storage (`data/mritidhristi_store.json`), and a 26-table relational PostgreSQL blueprint (`docs/database/schema.sql`) prepared for hosted database migration.\n\n### What Was Built\n1. **Three Role-Based Dashboards & RBAC**\n   - **Patient Dashboard**: Welcome banner, Prevent/Detect/Protect launch cards, 6-month Health Overview chart, Retinal Screening & Grad-CAM preview, 12-month Prevention Programme ring, Upcoming Appointments, Quick Actions, Health Insights, and right operational rail.\n   - **Doctor / Healthcare Worker Dashboard**: Pending retinal reviews queue, missed/escalated appointment alerts, and searchable shared longitudinal patient registry.\n   - **District Administrator Dashboard**: Data provenance banner, district KPIs, facility utilization & Simulink comparison charts, and security audit trail.\n   - **Role Switcher & Auth**: Instant synthetic role demo switcher (Patient / Doctor / Admin) plus email/password registration and sign-in.\n\n2. **Pillar 1 \342\200\224 PREVENT (Type 2 Diabetes Risk & Prevention)**\n   - **9-Input Wizard**: One-question-at-a-time lifestyle assessment (age, diet, sleep, physical activity/steps, weight, waist circumference, family history, smoking, alcohol) with an explicitly labelled *experimental rule-based score*, top 3 modifiable factors, and recommendations.\n   - **What-If Explorer**: Illustrative scenario sliders showing real-time experimental score changes.\n   - **12-Month Prevention Programme**: Phase 1 (Learning, Months 1\342\200\2236) & Phase 2 (Maintenance, Months 7\342\200\22312), Indian dietary guidance, daily habit check-ins, and a deterministic 5-step adaptive intervention ladder using pre-approved educational framing.\n   - **Clinical Testing & Registration**: HbA1c and Fasting Plasma Glucose guidance with doctor-only lab recording, plus patient registration with granular informed consent and English/Tamil language support (Hindi architecture scaffolded).\n\n3. **Pillar 2 \342\200\224 DETECT (AI-Assisted Diabetic Retinopathy Screening)**\n   - **Interactive 7-Step Retinal Pipeline**: Upload a fundus image or select from 3 procedural demo presets (*Normal Grade 0*, *Moderate NPDR*, *Ungradable Blur*).\n   - **Step 1 Quality Gate**: Live pixel-level sharpness (Laplacian variance), luminance, exposure clipping, resolution, and retinal color OOD checks that safely withhold grades and trigger recapture on ungradable inputs.\n   - **Explainability & Governance**: CLAHE preprocessing preview, optic disc/vessel & illustrative lesion overlays, Grad-CAM side-by-side viewer with opacity slider and explicit limitations, plus dataset governance specifications (APTOS 2019, IDRiD, DRIVE, Messidor-2).\n\n4. **Pillar 3 \342\200\224 PROTECT (Clinical Review, Referrals & Continuity of Care)**\n   - **Doctor Review & Triage Sign-Off**: Clinician-only Confirm / Reject / Recapture decisions, clinician-approved triage protocols, and clinical notes.\n   - **Referrals, Appointments & Follow-Ups**: Ophthalmology/endocrinology referral tracking, appointment booking with attendance and missed-visit escalation, and health-worker continuity follow-ups.\n\n5. **Offline-First PWA & Synchronization Engine**\n   - Installable PWA with in-app Install button (and iOS Safari Add-to-Home-Screen guide), live online/offline detection, and an **Offline Test Mode** toggle.\n   - Dexie.js IndexedDB caches minimized permitted records and queues offline Prevent actions (lifestyle assessments, habit logs, lesson completions) with unique idempotency keys that automatically sync and deduplicate upon reconnection.\n\n6. **District Resource Planning (MATLAB Simulink Interface)**\n   - Six district scenarios (*Normal*, *High Patient Volume*, *Limited Connectivity*, *Camera Shortage*, *Ophthalmologist Shortage*, *Increased Referral Demand*), hourly queue charts, cross-scenario comparison, downloadable CSV template, and Admin-only Simulink CSV import.\n\n### Verified Safeguards\n- **Server-enforced role access**: Backend APIs verify the caller\'s role and patient record ownership on every request (for example, a Patient session receives HTTP `403` when requesting admin audit logs, and denied attempts are recorded in the audit trail).\n- **Safe credential & session handling**: Passwords use per-user salted `scrypt` hashes with timing-safe comparison, and session tokens are kept strictly in client memory rather than browser local storage or IndexedDB.\n- **Validated inputs & deduplicated sync**: All API payloads and uploaded retinal images are validated server-side, and offline batch sync enforces idempotency keys so replayed actions are safely skipped without creating duplicate records.\n\n### How to Test\n- **Switch Roles**: Click your profile in the top right to switch between **Patient (Shwetha V)**, **Doctor (Dr. Arvind Raman)**, and **District Admin (Priya Natarajan)**, or test live backend permission blocking inside **Settings \342\206\222 Verify Backend RBAC**.\n- **Test Offline Sync**: Toggle **Offline Test Mode** in the top bar (or inside **Offline Sync**), submit a daily habit or 9-input assessment in **Prevent**, inspect the queued item in **Offline Sync**, then reconnect to watch automatic deduplicated sync.\n- **Test Quality Gate & Doctor Sign-Off**: Open **Detect**, run the **Ungradable Blur** preset to verify safe grade withholding, then run **Moderate NPDR** and switch to **Doctor** in **Protect** to complete clinical review and create an ophthalmology referral.\n\n### Prototype Boundaries & Next Phase Readiness\n- Lifestyle risk scoring, retinal AI grading/Grad-CAM visualizations, and default district capacity figures are **experimental/illustrative prototype outputs** using synthetic seed data \342\200\224 not clinically validated diagnostic models or live MATLAB execution.\n- All progress and the 26-table relational schema are documented in `PROJECT_PROGRESS.md` and `docs/database/schema.sql`. When you are ready to provision a hosted PostgreSQL database (Cloud SQL) or extend the Python FastAPI/PyTorch reference layer, let me know and we can proceed with the next phase."
    message_id: "pM8Ca8KeFf_d_uMP0KnykQg"
    modified_response: "**MRITIDHRISTI \342\200\223 PREVENT \342\200\242 DETECT \342\200\242 PROTECT** has been built and verified as an integrated, offline-first, role-based healthcare screening and continuity-of-care prototype.\n\n### Architecture Overview\n- **Frontend**: React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS v4, Recharts, Lucide icons, and Dexie.js (IndexedDB) configured as an installable Progressive Web App (`vite-plugin-pwa` + Workbox Service Worker + Web App Manifest).\n- **Backend**: Node.js + Express REST API on port `3000` serving the SPA, Zod request validation, role-based access control (`patient`, `doctor`, `admin`), salted `scrypt` password hashing, in-memory Bearer sessions, persistent JSON storage (`data/mritidhristi_store.json`), and a 26-table relational PostgreSQL blueprint (`docs/database/schema.sql`) prepared for hosted database migration.\n\n### What Was Built\n1. **Three Role-Based Dashboards & RBAC**\n   - **Patient Dashboard**: Welcome banner, Prevent/Detect/Protect launch cards, 6-month Health Overview chart, Retinal Screening & Grad-CAM preview, 12-month Prevention Programme ring, Upcoming Appointments, Quick Actions, Health Insights, and right operational rail.\n   - **Doctor / Healthcare Worker Dashboard**: Pending retinal reviews queue, missed/escalated appointment alerts, and searchable shared longitudinal patient registry.\n   - **District Administrator Dashboard**: Data provenance banner, district KPIs, facility utilization & Simulink comparison charts, and security audit trail.\n   - **Role Switcher & Auth**: Instant synthetic role demo switcher (Patient / Doctor / Admin) plus email/password registration and sign-in.\n\n2. **Pillar 1 \342\200\224 PREVENT (Type 2 Diabetes Risk & Prevention)**\n   - **9-Input Wizard**: One-question-at-a-time lifestyle assessment (age, diet, sleep, physical activity/steps, weight, waist circumference, family history, smoking, alcohol) with an explicitly labelled *experimental rule-based score*, top 3 modifiable factors, and recommendations.\n   - **What-If Explorer**: Illustrative scenario sliders showing real-time experimental score changes.\n   - **12-Month Prevention Programme**: Phase 1 (Learning, Months 1\342\200\2236) & Phase 2 (Maintenance, Months 7\342\200\22312), Indian dietary guidance, daily habit check-ins, and a deterministic 5-step adaptive intervention ladder using pre-approved educational framing.\n   - **Clinical Testing & Registration**: HbA1c and Fasting Plasma Glucose guidance with doctor-only lab recording, plus patient registration with granular informed consent and English/Tamil language support (Hindi architecture scaffolded).\n\n3. **Pillar 2 \342\200\224 DETECT (AI-Assisted Diabetic Retinopathy Screening)**\n   - **Interactive 7-Step Retinal Pipeline**: Upload a fundus image or select from 3 procedural demo presets (*Normal Grade 0*, *Moderate NPDR*, *Ungradable Blur*).\n   - **Step 1 Quality Gate**: Live pixel-level sharpness (Laplacian variance), luminance, exposure clipping, resolution, and retinal color OOD checks that safely withhold grades and trigger recapture on ungradable inputs.\n   - **Explainability & Governance**: CLAHE preprocessing preview, optic disc/vessel & illustrative lesion overlays, Grad-CAM side-by-side viewer with opacity slider and explicit limitations, plus dataset governance specifications (APTOS 2019, IDRiD, DRIVE, Messidor-2).\n\n4. **Pillar 3 \342\200\224 PROTECT (Clinical Review, Referrals & Continuity of Care)**\n   - **Doctor Review & Triage Sign-Off**: Clinician-only Confirm / Reject / Recapture decisions, clinician-approved triage protocols, and clinical notes.\n   - **Referrals, Appointments & Follow-Ups**: Ophthalmology/endocrinology referral tracking, appointment booking with attendance and missed-visit escalation, and health-worker continuity follow-ups.\n\n5. **Offline-First PWA & Synchronization Engine**\n   - Installable PWA with in-app Install button (and iOS Safari Add-to-Home-Screen guide), live online/offline detection, and an **Offline Test Mode** toggle.\n   - Dexie.js IndexedDB caches minimized permitted records and queues offline Prevent actions (lifestyle assessments, habit logs, lesson completions) with unique idempotency keys that automatically sync and deduplicate upon reconnection.\n\n6. **District Resource Planning (MATLAB Simulink Interface)**\n   - Six district scenarios (*Normal*, *High Patient Volume*, *Limited Connectivity*, *Camera Shortage*, *Ophthalmologist Shortage*, *Increased Referral Demand*), hourly queue charts, cross-scenario comparison, downloadable CSV template, and Admin-only Simulink CSV import.\n\n### Verified Safeguards\n- **Server-enforced role access**: Backend APIs verify the caller\'s role and patient record ownership on every request (for example, a Patient session receives HTTP `403` when requesting admin audit logs, and denied attempts are recorded in the audit trail).\n- **Safe credential & session handling**: Passwords use per-user salted `scrypt` hashes with timing-safe comparison, and session tokens are kept strictly in client memory rather than browser local storage or IndexedDB.\n- **Validated inputs & deduplicated sync**: All API payloads and uploaded retinal images are validated server-side, and offline batch sync enforces idempotency keys so replayed actions are safely skipped without creating duplicate records.\n\n### How to Test\n- **Switch Roles**: Click your profile in the top right to switch between **Patient (Shwetha V)**, **Doctor (Dr. Arvind Raman)**, and **District Admin (Priya Natarajan)**, or test live backend permission blocking inside **Settings \342\206\222 Verify Backend RBAC**.\n- **Test Offline Sync**: Toggle **Offline Test Mode** in the top bar (or inside **Offline Sync**), submit a daily habit or 9-input assessment in **Prevent**, inspect the queued item in **Offline Sync**, then reconnect to watch automatic deduplicated sync.\n- **Test Quality Gate & Doctor Sign-Off**: Open **Detect**, run the **Ungradable Blur** preset to verify safe grade withholding, then run **Moderate NPDR** and switch to **Doctor** in **Protect** to complete clinical review and create an ophthalmology referral.\n\n### Prototype Boundaries & Next Phase Readiness\n- Lifestyle risk scoring, retinal AI grading/Grad-CAM visualizations, and default district capacity figures are **experimental/illustrative prototype outputs** using synthetic seed data \342\200\224 not clinically validated diagnostic models or live MATLAB execution.\n- All progress and the 26-table relational schema are documented in `PROJECT_PROGRESS.md` and `docs/database/schema.sql`. When you are ready to provision a hosted PostgreSQL database (Cloud SQL) or extend the Python FastAPI/PyTorch reference layer, let me know and we can proceed with the next phase."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\253\005\n\250\005\001i\024}\023a\237\355\262\0357\231V/\327\f\361\327\256WO\2509\3137\317\250\312\304\250\3427\372-\365h(\333Vt\327\235\317\241\204y\315\203zI\3660\'Pp\016\237=\016\037s\266V\'\252{\026\215\032.\247\a\217\001f_9\323\262\315RVH\257)\003|\240p6;\241\337\351b9IY\035\316\017\341\254[$*\025\235F\260\215~I\031\312;\222x<\030\313\245<\240\312?\026I9\036C6Ia}\\\'\211\237t\"\224\017,\213\276\317\261\020M\2257\030\3543\274\262+\335,\234<\003i>\v\267\206\340I\200\347\224\030^\263V\266v\312\231@\"\237\023\"\346I\206\026\372U\362\021\300=\311i/5\202\205\345\035\301\243\203\003_\202\026\272 \320\324fbA5\266\vC\354\207\325q5\273\203\t>\320\t\366g\350\367[\025\312\336\350L\211\237\234s\"I\350\030#\362\240\'\331R\v\024\375\360Fi\353\b\0053C\226\252\224^\273\302\247\304\377@8</Q\020\255\003\272\324\252\220\333R`\222W\243\260\357\3138\373tiWU\346t>\307\372\307\240\337\240\340\265/\210\300\206U<\340\333\177X\"<\352|nq\307\314\a_\270\370\026\326\034:\213\027\245\024\347m\\\326u\235\274\253Y.\224\221i\317ab\247a\027\203\335a9\312\3272sE9f\243\256L\355\2404\306\224k?\350\271cu;\343&\2664\345~\302qn\205\231\345\345\2526\234#\357*\373whFM\251G\322\201\017I\246\23512\217\316\344\357\306\307\233iD\'r\036\322v3\303R\263\000\316\023\224~\224\242hH\306\225V=\305\327\246\002\027J\346N\273\0356Z6\336\254\030\231\230\235k\345\347\254p\242\277\215\372a$\302\237d\231\265\373\341\203\331\353j\205\215\322\377\312\346\340\252\254\n\256\325\226\326\377\241\344\302l\202#Ob\360\200\332\\\335\361az\3019\220\301m\310\366u\312\222\231\330\202\304\222l\037\300=\205I\310\035\345/t(\347\341X\270\\\230\307\265g\276\354\251\363~K\003\335\023\036fn\355\261_]\374\344k\270\314\376\245U?F\333\263\365\252\205\023\202\203\265m1;\271$\307G\220\363\300Q\236\222#\304\357\250\237\361\210\314l!\316Q\303\365\214\334\305\266\000?\3571\253O\243\262\316\020\356Z\264\333*\351\004E\377\t\217\351\036|qFe\367B!\334+s\252\275\211\333g\251\260a\023\277\262\020\247Jz \347\264"
